#: src/introduction.md:1
msgid ""
"**Note:** Impatient readers may head straight to [Quick Start](quick-start."
"md)."
msgstr "**注意：** 不耐烦的读者可以直接跳到 [快速开始](quick-start.md)。"

#: src/introduction.md:3
msgid ""
"**Using previous version of Kubebuilder v1 or v2?** **Check the legacy "
"documentation for [v1](https://book-v1.book.kubebuilder.io), [v2](https://"
"book-v2.book.kubebuilder.io) or [v3](https://book-v3.book.kubebuilder.io)**"
msgstr "**使用旧版本的 Kubebuilder v1 或 v2？** **请查看 [v1](https://book-v1.book.kubebuilder.io)、[v2](https://book-v2.book.kubebuilder.io) 或 [v3](https://book-v3.book.kubebuilder.io) 的遗留文档**"

#: src/introduction.md:6
msgid "Who is this for"
msgstr "这适合谁"

#: src/introduction.md:8
msgid "Users of Kubernetes"
msgstr "Kubernetes的用户"

#: src/introduction.md:10
msgid ""
"Users of Kubernetes will develop a deeper understanding of Kubernetes "
"through learning the fundamental concepts behind how APIs are designed and "
"implemented.  This book will teach readers how to develop their own "
"Kubernetes APIs and the principles from which the core Kubernetes APIs are "
"designed."
msgstr "Kubernetes 用户将通过学习 API 设计和实现的基本概念，深入理解 Kubernetes。 本书将教会读者如何开发自己的 Kubernetes API 以及核心 Kubernetes API 设计的原则。"

#: src/introduction.md:15 src/introduction.md:31
msgid "Including:"
msgstr "包括："

#: src/introduction.md:17
msgid "The structure of Kubernetes APIs and Resources"
msgstr "Kubernetes API 和资源的结构"

#: src/introduction.md:18
msgid "API versioning semantics"
msgstr "API版本控制语义"

#: src/introduction.md:19
msgid "Self-healing"
msgstr "自我修复"

#: src/introduction.md:20
msgid "Garbage Collection and Finalizers"
msgstr "垃圾收集与终结器"

#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid "Declarative vs Imperative APIs"
msgstr "声明式 API 与 命令式 API"

#: src/introduction.md:22
msgid "Level-Based vs Edge-Base APIs"
msgstr "基于层级的 API 与基于边缘的 API"

#: src/introduction.md:23
msgid "Resources vs Subresources"
msgstr "资源与子资源"

#: src/introduction.md:25
msgid "Kubernetes API extension developers"
msgstr "Kubernetes API 扩展开发者"

#: src/introduction.md:27
msgid ""
"API extension developers will learn the principles and concepts behind "
"implementing canonical Kubernetes APIs, as well as simple tools and "
"libraries for rapid execution.  This book covers pitfalls and misconceptions "
"that extension developers commonly encounter."
msgstr "API 扩展开发者将学习实现规范 Kubernetes API 的原则和概念，以及用于快速执行的简单工具和库。 本书涵盖了扩展开发者常遇到的陷阱和误解。"

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid "How to batch multiple events into a single reconciliation call"
msgstr "如何将多个事件批量合并到一次对账调用中"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid "How to configure periodic reconciliation"
msgstr "如何配置定期对账"

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid "_Forthcoming_"
msgstr "_即将到来_"

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "When to use the lister cache vs live lookups"
msgstr "何时使用列出缓存与实时查找"

#: src/introduction.md:37
msgid "Garbage Collection vs Finalizers"
msgstr "垃圾回收与终结器"

#: src/introduction.md:38
msgid "How to use Declarative vs Webhook Validation"
msgstr "如何使用声明式验证与 Webhook 验证"

#: src/introduction.md:39
msgid "How to implement API versioning"
msgstr "如何实现 API 版本控制"

#: src/introduction.md:41
msgid "Why Kubernetes APIs"
msgstr "为什么选择 Kubernetes API"

#: src/introduction.md:43
msgid ""
"Kubernetes APIs provide consistent and well defined endpoints for objects "
"adhering to a consistent and rich structure."
msgstr "Kubernetes API 提供了一致且明确定义的对象网络端点，遵循一致且丰富的结构"

#: src/introduction.md:46
msgid ""
"This approach has fostered a rich ecosystem of tools and libraries for "
"working with Kubernetes APIs."
msgstr "这种方式促进了丰富的工具和库生态系统与 Kubernetes API 进行交互。"

#: src/introduction.md:49
msgid ""
"Users work with the APIs through declaring objects as _yaml_ or _json_ "
"config, and using common tooling to manage the objects."
msgstr "用户通过将对象声明为 _yaml_ 或 _json_ 配置，并使用常见工具来管理这些对象，方便与 APIs 进行交互。"

#: src/introduction.md:52
msgid ""
"Building services as Kubernetes APIs provides many advantages to plain old "
"REST, including:"
msgstr "将服务构建为 Kubernetes API 相较于传统的REST，有以下优势："

#: src/introduction.md:54
msgid "Hosted API endpoints, storage, and validation."
msgstr "托管的 API 网络端点、存储和验证。"

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid "Rich tooling and CLIs such as `kubectl` and `kustomize`."
msgstr "丰富的工具和命令行接口，例如 `kubectl` 和 `kustomize`。"

#: src/introduction.md:56
msgid "Support for AuthN and granular AuthZ."
msgstr "支持身份验证（AuthN）和细粒度授权（AuthZ）。"

#: src/introduction.md:57
msgid "Support for API evolution through API versioning and conversion."
msgstr "通过 API 版本控制和转换并且支持 API 版本演进。"

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid ""
"Facilitation of adaptive / self-healing APIs that continuously respond to "
"changes in the system state without user intervention."
msgstr "促进自适应/自愈 API 的实现，它们能够在没有用户干预的情况下持续响应系统状态的变化。"

#: src/introduction.md:60
msgid "Kubernetes as a hosting environment"
msgstr "Kubernetes 是一个托管环境"

#: src/introduction.md:62
msgid ""
"Developers may build and publish their own Kubernetes APIs for installation "
"into running Kubernetes clusters."
msgstr "开发者可以构建并发布自己的 Kubernetes API，方便安装到运行中的 Kubernetes 集群中。"

#: src/introduction.md:65
msgid "Contribution"
msgstr "贡献"

#: src/introduction.md:67
msgid ""
"If you like to contribute to either this book or the code, please be so kind "
"to read our [Contribution](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/"
"blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md) guidelines first."
msgstr "如果您希望为本书或代码贡献内容，请先阅读我们的[贡献](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubebuilder/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)指南。"

#: src/introduction.md:70
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "资源"

#: src/introduction.md:72
msgid "Repository: [sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder)"
msgstr "仓库: [sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder](https://sigs.k8s.io/kubebuilder)"

#: src/introduction.md:74
msgid "Slack channel: [\\#kubebuilder](http://slack.k8s.io/#kubebuilder)"
msgstr "Slack频道：[\\#kubebuilder](http://slack.k8s.io/#kubebuilder)"

#: src/introduction.md:76
msgid ""
"Google Group: [kubebuilder@googlegroups.com](https://groups.google.com/forum/"
"#!forum/kubebuilder)"
msgstr "Google 群组: [kubebuilder@googlegroups.com](https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/kubebuilder)"

