#: src/cronjob-tutorial/empty-main.md:5
msgid "With that out of the way, we can get on to scaffolding our API!"
msgstr "解决了这个问题后，我们可以开始搭建我们的 API 了！"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:3
msgid ""
"Before we get started with our API, we should talk about terminology a bit."
msgstr "在我们开始使用 API 之前，应该先聊聊一些术语。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:6
msgid ""
"When we talk about APIs in Kubernetes, we often use 4 terms: _groups_, "
"_versions_, _kinds_, and _resources_."
msgstr "在讨论 Kubernetes 中的 API 时，我们经常使用四个术语：_组_、_版本_、_种类_和_资源_。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:9
msgid "Groups and Versions"
msgstr "组和版本"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:11
msgid ""
"An _API Group_ in Kubernetes is simply a collection of related "
"functionality.  Each group has one or more _versions_, which, as the name "
"suggests, allow us to change how an API works over time."
msgstr "Kubernetes 中的 _API 组_ 只是相关功能的集合。每个组都有一个或多个 _版本_，顾名思义，这些版本允许我们随着时间的推移改变 API 的工作方式。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:15
msgid "Kinds and Resources"
msgstr "种类和资源"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:17
msgid ""
"Each API group-version contains one or more API types, which we call "
"_Kinds_.  While a Kind may change forms between versions, each form must be "
"able to store all the data of the other forms, somehow (we can store the "
"data in fields, or in annotations).  This means that using an older API "
"version won't cause newer data to be lost or corrupted.  See the [Kubernetes "
"API guidelines](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-"
"architecture/api-conventions.md) for more information."
msgstr "每个 API 组版本包含一个或多个 API 类型，我们称之为 _Kinds_。虽然一个 Kind 可能在不同版本之间改变形式，但每种形式必须能够以某种方式存储其他形式的所有数据（我们可以将数据存储在字段中或注释中）。这意味着使用旧的 API 版本不会导致较新的数据丢失或损坏。有关更多信息，请参阅 [Kubernetes API 指南](https://git.k8s.io/community/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md)。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:26
msgid ""
"You'll also hear mention of _resources_ on occasion.  A resource is simply a "
"use of a Kind in the API.  Often, there's a one-to-one mapping between Kinds "
"and resources.  For instance, the `pods` resource corresponds to the `Pod` "
"Kind.  However, sometimes, the same Kind may be returned by multiple "
"resources.  For instance, the `Scale` Kind is returned by all scale "
"subresources, like `deployments/scale` or `replicasets/scale`.  This is what "
"allows the Kubernetes HorizontalPodAutoscaler to interact with different "
"resources.  With CRDs, however, each Kind will correspond to a single "
"resource."
msgstr "您有时还会听到提到 _资源_。资源只是 API 中对 Kind 的一种使用。通常，Kinds 和资源之间存在一对一的映射关系。例如，`pods` 资源对应于 `Pod` Kind。然而，有时候，同一个 Kind 可能会由多个资源返回。例如，`Scale` Kind 会由所有缩放子资源返回，如 `deployments/scale` 或 `replicasets/scale`。这使得 Kubernetes 的 HorizontalPodAutoscaler 能够与不同的资源进行交互。然而，对于自定义资源定义（CRDs）而言，每个 Kind 将对应一个单一的资源。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:36
msgid ""
"Notice that resources are always lowercase, and by convention are the "
"lowercase form of the Kind."
msgstr "请注意，资源始终使用小写字母，并且根据惯例，它们是 Kind 的小写形式。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:39
msgid "So, how does that correspond to Go?"
msgstr "那么，这与围棋有什么关系呢？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:41
msgid ""
"When we refer to a kind in a particular group version, we'll call it a "
"_GroupVersionKind_, or GVK for short.  Same with resources and GVR. As we'll "
"see shortly, each GVK corresponds to a given root Go type in a package."
msgstr "当我们在特定组版本中提到一种类型时，我们将其称为 _GroupVersionKind_，简称 GVK。资源同样适用 GVR。正如我们稍后将看到的，每个 GVK 对应于一个包中的特定根 Go 类型。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:46
msgid ""
"Now that we have our terminology straight, we can _actually_ create our API!"
msgstr "现在我们把术语理顺了，可以_真正_创建我们的 API 了！"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:49
msgid "So, how can we create our API?"
msgstr "那么，我们该如何创建我们的 API 呢？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:51
msgid ""
"In the next section, [Adding a new API](../cronjob-tutorial/new-api.html), "
"we will check how the tool helps us to create our own APIs with the command "
"`kubebuilder create api`."
msgstr "在下一部分[添加新的 API](../cronjob-tutorial/new-api.html)中，我们将检查该工具如何通过命令 `kubebuilder create api` 帮助我们创建自己的 API。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:54
msgid ""
"The goal of this command is to create a Custom Resource (CR) and Custom "
"Resource Definition (CRD) for our Kind(s). To check it further see; [Extend "
"the Kubernetes API with CustomResourceDefinitions](https://kubernetes.io/"
"docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/)."
msgstr "此命令的目标是为我们的类型创建一个自定义资源（CR）和自定义资源定义（CRD）。要进一步了解，请参见：[使用自定义资源定义扩展Kubernetes API](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/)。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:56
msgid "But, why create APIs at all?"
msgstr "但是，为什么要创建API呢？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:58
msgid ""
"New APIs are how we teach Kubernetes about our custom objects. The Go "
"structs are used to generate a CRD which includes the schema for our data as "
"well as tracking data like what our new type is called. We can then create "
"instances of our custom objects which will be managed by our [controllers]"
"(../cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md)."
msgstr "新的 API 是我们向 Kubernetes 教授自定义对象的方式。Go 结构体用于生成 CRD，包含我们数据的架构以及跟踪诸如新类型名称等数据。然后，我们可以创建自定义对象的实例，这些实例将由我们的 [控制器](../cronjob-tutorial/controller-overview.md) 进行管理。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:60
msgid ""
"Our APIs and resources represent our solutions on the clusters. Basically, "
"the CRDs are a definition of our customized Objects, and the CRs are an "
"instance of it."
msgstr "我们的 API 和资源代表了我们在集群上的解决方案。基本上，CRD（自定义资源定义）是我们自定义对象的定义，而 CR（自定义资源）是其实例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:62
msgid "Ah, do you have an example?"
msgstr "啊，你有例子吗？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:64
msgid ""
"Let’s think about the classic scenario where the goal is to have an "
"application and its database running on the platform with Kubernetes. Then, "
"one CRD could represent the App, and another one could represent the DB. By "
"having one CRD to describe the App and another one for the DB, we will not "
"be hurting concepts such as encapsulation, the single responsibility "
"principle, and cohesion. Damaging these concepts could cause unexpected side "
"effects, such as difficulty in extending, reuse, or maintenance, just to "
"mention a few."
msgstr "让我们想一想经典场景，目标是在平台上运行应用程序及其数据库，使用 Kubernetes。在这个场景中，一个 CRD 可以表示应用程序，而另一个 CRD 可以表示数据库。通过为应用程序创建一个 CRD，并为数据库创建另一个 CRD，我们不会损害诸如封装、单一职责原则和内聚性等概念。损害这些概念可能会导致意想不到的副作用，例如在扩展、重用或维护方面遇到困难，仅举几例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:66
msgid ""
"In this way, we can create the App CRD which will have its controller and "
"which would be responsible for things like creating Deployments that contain "
"the App and creating Services to access it and etc. Similarly, we could "
"create a CRD to represent the DB, and deploy a controller that would manage "
"DB instances."
msgstr "通过这种方式，我们可以创建应用程序的 CRD，它将拥有自己的控制器，负责诸如创建包含应用程序的 Deployment、创建访问该应用程序的 Service 等。类似地，我们可以创建一个 CRD 来表示数据库，并部署一个控制器来管理数据库实例。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:68
msgid "Err, but what's that Scheme thing?"
msgstr "呃，但那个Scheme是什么东西？"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:70
msgid ""
"The `Scheme` we saw before is simply a way to keep track of what Go type "
"corresponds to a given GVK (don't be overwhelmed by its [godocs](https://pkg."
"go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme))."
msgstr "我们之前看到的 `Scheme` 只是一个用来跟踪给定 GVK 对应的 Go 类型的方式（不要被它的 [godocs](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime?tab=doc#Scheme) 压倒）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:74
msgid ""
"For instance, suppose we mark the `\"tutorial.kubebuilder.io/api/v1\"."
"CronJob{}` type as being in the `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1` API group "
"(implicitly saying it has the Kind `CronJob`)."
msgstr "例如，假设我们将 `\"tutorial.kubebuilder.io/api/v1\".CronJob{}` 类型标记为属于 `batch.tutorial.kubebuilder.io/v1` API 组（隐含地表示它的 Kind 为 `CronJob`）。"

#: src/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.md:79
msgid ""
"Then, we can later construct a new `&CronJob{}` given some JSON from the API "
"server that says"
msgstr "然后，我们可以根据API服务器提供的JSON数据，稍后构建一个新的 `&CronJob{}`。"

