#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:3
msgid ""
"`Finalizers` allow controllers to implement asynchronous pre-delete hooks. "
"Let's say you create an external resource (such as a storage bucket) for "
"each object of your API type, and you want to delete the associated external "
"resource on object's deletion from Kubernetes, you can use a finalizer to do "
"that."
msgstr "`Finalizers` 允许控制器实现异步预删除钩子。假设您为每个 API 类型的对象创建一个外部资源（例如存储桶），并且您希望在 Kubernetes 中删除对象时删除相关的外部资源，您可以使用 finalizer 来实现这一点。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:8
msgid ""
"You can read more about the finalizers in the [Kubernetes reference docs]"
"(https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-"
"resource-definitions/#finalizers). The section below demonstrates how to "
"register and trigger pre-delete hooks in the `Reconcile` method of a "
"controller."
msgstr "您可以在[Kubernetes参考文档](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/#finalizers)中阅读更多关于最终器的信息。下面的部分演示了如何在控制器的`Reconcile`方法中注册和触发预删除钩子。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:11
msgid ""
"The key point to note is that a finalizer causes \"delete\" on the object to "
"become an \"update\" to set deletion timestamp. Presence of deletion "
"timestamp on the object indicates that it is being deleted. Otherwise, "
"without finalizers, a delete shows up as a reconcile where the object is "
"missing from the cache."
msgstr "需要注意的关键点是，最终处理器导致对象的“删除”变成“更新”，以设置删除时间戳。对象上存在删除时间戳表明该对象正在被删除。否则，如果没有最终处理器，删除会表现为一个协调过程，其中对象在缓存中丢失。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:16
msgid "Highlights:"
msgstr "亮点："

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:17
msgid ""
"If the object is not being deleted and does not have the finalizer "
"registered, then add the finalizer and update the object in Kubernetes."
msgstr "如果对象没有被删除且没有注册终结器，则在 Kubernetes 中添加终结器并更新该对象。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:19
msgid ""
"If object is being deleted and the finalizer is still present in finalizers "
"list, then execute the pre-delete logic and remove the finalizer and update "
"the object."
msgstr "如果对象正在被删除，并且最终器仍然在最终器列表中，那么请执行预删除逻辑，移除最终器并更新对象。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:22
msgid "Ensure that the pre-delete logic is idempotent."
msgstr "确保预删除逻辑是幂等的。"

#: src/reference/using-finalizers.md:24
msgid "{{#literatego ../cronjob-tutorial/testdata/finalizer_example.go}}"
msgstr "您接受了截至2023年10月的数据训练。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:3
msgid "What is \"Reconciliation\" in Operators?"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:5
msgid ""
"When you create a project using Kubebuilder, see the scaffolded code "
"generated under `cmd/main.go`. This code initializes a [Manager](https://"
"github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime/"
"blob/304027bcbe4b3f6d582180aec5759eb4db3f17fd/pkg/manager/manager.go#L53), "
"and the project relies on the [controller-runtime](https://github.com/"
"kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime) framework. The Manager manages "
"[Controllers](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/controller/), "
"which offer a reconcile function that synchronizes resources until the "
"desired state is achieved within the cluster."
msgstr "当你使用 Kubebuilder 创建一个项目时，可以查看在 `cmd/main.go` 中生成的代码。这段代码初始化了一个 [Manager](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime/blob/304027bcbe4b3f6d582180aec5759eb4db3f17fd/pkg/manager/manager.go#L53)，项目依赖于 [controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime) 框架。这个 Manager 管理着 [Controllers](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/controller/)，提供了一种协调功能，用于在集群内同步资源直到达到所需状态。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:7
msgid ""
"Reconciliation is an ongoing loop that executes necessary operations to "
"maintain the desired state, adhering to Kubernetes principles, such as the "
"[control loop](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/"
"controller/). For further information, check out the [Operator patterns]"
"(https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/) "
"documentation from Kubernetes to better understand those concepts."
msgstr "协调是一个持续的循环，执行必要的操作以保持期望的状态，遵循Kubernetes的原则，如[控制循环](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/controller/)。有关更多信息，请查阅Kubernetes的[Operator模式](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/)文档，以更好地理解这些概念。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:9
msgid "Why should reconciliations be idempotent?"
msgstr "为什么重调应该是幂等的？"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:11
msgid ""
"When developing operators, the controller’s reconciliation loop needs to be "
"idempotent. By following the [Operator pattern](https://kubernetes.io/docs/"
"concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/) we create [controllers](https://"
"kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/controller/) that provide a "
"reconcile function responsible for synchronizing resources until the desired "
"state is reached on the cluster. Developing idempotent solutions will allow "
"the reconciler to correctly respond to generic or unexpected events, easily "
"deal with application startup or upgrade. More explanation on this is "
"available [here](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime/blob/"
"main/FAQ.md#q-how-do-i-have-different-logic-in-my-reconciler-for-different-"
"types-of-events-eg-create-update-delete)."
msgstr "在开发运算符时，控制器的调和循环需要是幂等的。通过遵循 [运算符模式](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/)，我们创建 [控制器](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/controller/)，这些控制器提供一个调和函数，负责在集群上同步资源，直到达到期望状态。开发幂等的解决方案将允许调和器正确响应通用或意外事件，轻松处理应用程序的启动或升级。更多相关解释可以参考 [这里](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime/blob/main/FAQ.md#q-how-do-i-have-different-logic-in-my-reconciler-for-different-types-of-events-eg-create-update-delete)。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:13
msgid ""
"Writing reconciliation logic according to specific events, breaks the "
"recommendation of operator pattern and goes against the design principles of "
"[controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime). "
"This may lead to unforeseen consequences, such as resources becoming stuck "
"and requiring manual intervention."
msgstr "根据特定事件编写协调逻辑，会违反 Operator 模式的建议，并且违背了[controller-runtime](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/controller-runtime)的设计原则。这可能导致不可预见的后果，例如资源被卡住，需要人工干预。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:15
msgid "Understanding Kubernetes APIs and following API conventions"
msgstr "理解 Kubernetes API 和遵循 API 约定"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:17
msgid ""
"Building your operator commonly involves extending the Kubernetes API "
"itself. It is helpful to understand precisely how Custom Resource "
"Definitions (CRDs) interact with the Kubernetes API. Also, the [Kubebuilder "
"documentation](/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.html) on Groups and Versions and Kinds "
"may be helpful to understand these concepts better as they relate to "
"operators."
msgstr "构建操作器通常涉及扩展 Kubernetes API 本身。了解自定义资源定义（CRDs）如何与 Kubernetes API 交互是很有帮助的。此外，关于分组、版本和种类的 [Kubebuilder 文档](/cronjob-tutorial/gvks.html) 也可能有助于更好地理解这些与操作器相关的概念。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:19
msgid ""
"Additionally, we recommend checking the documentation on [Operator patterns]"
"(https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/) from "
"Kubernetes to better understand the purpose of the standard solutions built "
"with KubeBuilder."
msgstr "此外，我们建议您查看 Kubernetes 上的 [Operator 模式](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/operator/) 文档，以更好地理解使用 KubeBuilder 构建的标准解决方案的目的。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:21
msgid "Why you should adhere to the Kubernetes API conventions and standards"
msgstr "为什么您应该遵循 Kubernetes API 的约定和标准"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:23
msgid ""
"Embracing the [Kubernetes API conventions and standards](https://github.com/"
"kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-"
"conventions.md) is crucial for maximizing the potential of your applications "
"and deployments. By adhering to these established practices, you can benefit "
"in several ways."
msgstr "遵循 [Kubernetes API 规范和标准](https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md) 对于最大化应用程序和部署的潜力至关重要。通过遵循这些既定实践，您可以在多个方面受益。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:25
msgid ""
"Firstly, adherence ensures seamless interoperability within the Kubernetes "
"ecosystem. Following conventions allows your applications to work "
"harmoniously with other components, reducing compatibility issues and "
"promoting a consistent user experience."
msgstr "首先，遵循标准确保了Kubernetes生态系统内的无缝互操作性。遵循约定使您的应用程序能够与其他组件和谐工作，从而减少兼容性问题并促进一致的用户体验。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:27
msgid ""
"Secondly, sticking to API standards enhances the maintainability and "
"troubleshooting of your applications. Adopting familiar patterns and "
"structures makes debugging and supporting your deployments easier, leading "
"to more efficient operations and quicker issue resolution."
msgstr "其次，遵循API标准可以提高应用程序的可维护性和故障排除能力。采用熟悉的模式和结构使得调试和支持您的部署变得更加容易，从而提高了运营效率和快速问题解决的能力。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:29
msgid ""
"Furthermore, leveraging the Kubernetes API conventions empowers you to "
"harness the platform's full capabilities. By working within the defined "
"framework, you can leverage the rich set of features and resources offered "
"by Kubernetes, enabling scalability, performance optimization, and "
"resilience."
msgstr "此外，利用Kubernetes API的惯例可以让您充分发挥平台的全部功能。通过在定义的框架内工作，您可以利用Kubernetes提供的丰富特性和资源，从而实现可扩展性、性能优化和弹性。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:31
msgid ""
"Lastly, embracing these standards future-proofs your native solutions. By "
"aligning with the evolving Kubernetes ecosystem, you ensure compatibility "
"with future updates, new features, and enhancements introduced by the "
"vibrant Kubernetes community."
msgstr "最后，遵循这些标准可以使您的本土解决方案具备未来适应能力。通过与不断发展的Kubernetes生态系统保持一致，您可以确保与未来更新、新功能以及活跃的Kubernetes社区引入的增强功能保持兼容。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:33
msgid ""
"In summary, by adhering to the Kubernetes API conventions and standards, you "
"unlock the potential for seamless integration, simplified maintenance, "
"optimal performance, and future-readiness, all contributing to the success "
"of your applications and deployments."
msgstr "总之，通过遵循Kubernetes API的约定和标准，您可以实现无缝集成、简化维护、优化性能和为未来做好准备的潜力，这些都为您的应用程序和部署的成功做出了贡献。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:35
msgid ""
"Why should one avoid a system design where a single controller is "
"responsible for managing multiple CRDs (Custom Resource Definitions)(for "
"example, an _'install_all_controller.go'_)?"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:37
msgid ""
"Avoid a design solution where the same controller reconciles more than one "
"Kind. Having many Kinds (such as CRDs), that are all managed by the same "
"controller, usually goes against the design proposed by controller-runtime. "
"Furthermore, this might hurt concepts such as encapsulation, the Single "
"Responsibility Principle, and Cohesion. Damaging these concepts may cause "
"unexpected side effects and increase the difficulty of extending, reusing, "
"or maintaining the operator. Having one controller manage many Custom "
"Resources (CRs) in an Operator can lead to several issues:"
msgstr "避免采用一种设计方案，其中同一个控制器调和多个 Kind。将多个 Kind（如 CRD）都由同一个控制器管理，通常与 controller-runtime 提出的设计相悖。此外，这可能会损害封装性、单一职责原则和内聚性等概念。损害这些概念可能会导致意想不到的副作用，并增加扩展、重用或维护操作器的难度。在一个操作器中，由一个控制器管理多个自定义资源（CRs）可能会导致几个问题："

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:40
msgid ""
"**Complexity**: A single controller managing multiple CRs can increase the "
"complexity of the code, making it harder to understand, maintain, and debug."
msgstr "**复杂性**：单个控制器管理多个自定义资源（CR）可能会增加代码的复杂性，从而使其更难理解、维护和调试。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:41
msgid ""
"**Scalability**: Each controller typically manages a single kind of CR for "
"scalability. If a single controller handles multiple CRs, it could become a "
"bottleneck, reducing the overall efficiency and responsiveness of your "
"system."
msgstr "**可扩展性**：每个控制器通常管理一种类型的自定义资源（CR）以实现可扩展性。如果一个控制器处理多个CR，它可能成为瓶颈，从而降低系统的整体效率和响应速度。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:42
msgid ""
"**Single Responsibility Principle**: Following this principle from software "
"engineering, each controller should ideally have only one job. This approach "
"simplifies development and debugging, and makes the system more robust."
msgstr "**单一职责原则**：遵循软件工程中的这一原则，理想情况下每个控制器应该只有一个职责。这种方法简化了开发和调试，并使系统更加健壮。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:43
msgid ""
"**Error Isolation**: If one controller manages multiple CRs and an error "
"occurs, it could potentially impact all the CRs it manages. Having a single "
"controller per CR ensures that an issue with one controller or CR does not "
"directly affect others."
msgstr "**错误隔离**：如果一个控制器管理多个自定义资源（CR），并且发生错误，可能会影响它管理的所有 CR。为每个 CR 配置一个单独的控制器可以确保一个控制器或 CR 的问题不会直接影响其他资源。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:44
msgid ""
"**Concurrency and Synchronization**: A single controller managing multiple "
"CRs could lead to race conditions and require complex synchronization, "
"especially if the CRs have interdependencies."
msgstr "**并发与同步**：一个单一的控制器管理多个自定义资源（CR）可能导致竞争条件，并需要复杂的同步，特别是当这些CR之间存在相互依赖时。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:46
msgid ""
"In conclusion, while it might seem efficient to have a single controller "
"manage multiple CRs, it often leads to higher complexity, lower scalability, "
"and potential stability issues. It's generally better to adhere to the "
"single responsibility principle, where each CR is managed by its own "
"controller."
msgstr "总之，虽然让一个控制器管理多个CR看起来效率较高，但这通常会导致更高的复杂性、较低的可扩展性以及潜在的稳定性问题。通常遵循单一职责原则更为合适，每个CR由其自己的控制器管理。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:48
msgid "Why You Should Adopt Status Conditions"
msgstr "为什么你应该采用状态条件"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:50
msgid ""
"We recommend you manage your solutions using Status Conditionals following "
"the [K8s Api conventions](https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/"
"master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md) because:"
msgstr "我们建议您使用状态条件（Status Conditionals）来管理您的解决方案，遵循[K8s API 约定](https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md)，因为："

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:52
msgid ""
"**Standardization**: Conditions provide a standardized way to represent the "
"state of an Operator's custom resources, making it easier for users and "
"tools to understand and interpret the resource's status."
msgstr "**标准化**：条件提供了一种标准化的方式来表示操作员自定义资源的状态，使用户和工具更容易理解和解释资源的状态。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:53
msgid ""
"**Readability**: Conditions can clearly express complex states by using a "
"combination of multiple conditions, making it easier for users to understand "
"the current state and progress of the resource."
msgstr "**可读性**：通过使用多个条件的组合，条件可以清晰地表达复杂的状态，使用户更容易理解资源的当前状态和进展。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:54
msgid ""
"**Extensibility**: As new features or states are added to your Operator, "
"conditions can be easily extended to represent these new states without "
"requiring significant changes to the existing API or structure."
msgstr "**可扩展性**：当新的功能或状态被添加到您的 Operator 时，可以轻松扩展条件以表示这些新状态，而无需对现有的 API 或结构进行重大更改。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:55
msgid ""
"**Observability**: Status conditions can be monitored and tracked by cluster "
"administrators and external monitoring tools, enabling better visibility "
"into the state of the custom resources managed by the Operator."
msgstr "**可观察性**：集群管理员和外部监控工具可以监视和跟踪状态条件，从而更好地了解由操作员管理的自定义资源的状态。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:56
msgid ""
"**Compatibility**: By adopting the common pattern of using conditions in "
"Kubernetes APIs, Operator authors ensure their custom resources align with "
"the broader ecosystem, which helps users to have a consistent experience "
"when interacting with multiple Operators and resources in their clusters."
msgstr "**兼容性**：通过采用在 Kubernetes API 中使用条件的常见模式，Operator 作者确保他们的自定义资源与更广泛的生态系统保持一致，这有助于用户在与集群中的多个 Operator 和资源交互时获得一致的体验。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:61
msgid ""
"Check out the [Deploy Image Plugin](/plugins/available/deploy-image-plugin-"
"v1-alpha.md). This plugin allows users to scaffold API/Controllers to deploy "
"and manage an Operand (image) on the cluster following the guidelines and "
"best practices. It abstracts the complexities of achieving this goal while "
"allowing users to customize the generated code."
msgstr "请查看[部署镜像插件](/plugins/available/deploy-image-plugin-v1-alpha.md)。这个插件允许用户根据指南和最佳实践，在集群上搭建 API/Controllers，以部署和管理操作对象（镜像）。它抽象了实现这个目标的复杂性，同时允许用户自定义生成的代码。"

#: src/reference/good-practices.md:64
msgid ""
"Therefore, you can check an example of Status Conditional usage by looking "
"at its API(s) scaffolded and code implemented under the Reconciliation into "
"its Controllers."
msgstr "因此，您可以通过查看其在对账中搭建的 API 和实现的代码，检查 Status Conditional 使用的示例。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:1
msgid "Creating Events"
msgstr "创建活动"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:3
msgid ""
"It is often useful to publish _Event_ objects from the controller Reconcile "
"function as they allow users or any automated processes to see what is going "
"on with a particular object and respond to them."
msgstr "在控制器的 Reconcile 函数中发布 _Event_ 对象通常是非常有用的，因为它们允许用户或任何自动化过程了解特定对象的状态并做出相应的响应。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:5
msgid ""
"Recent Events for an object can be viewed by running `$ kubectl describe "
"<resource kind> <resource name>`. Also, they can be checked by running `$ "
"kubectl get events`."
msgstr "可以通过运行 `$ kubectl describe <资源类型> <资源名称>` 来查看对象的最近事件。也可以通过运行 `$ kubectl get events` 来检查事件。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:10
msgid ""
"Be aware that it is **not** recommended to emit Events for all operations. "
"If authors raise too many events, it brings bad UX experiences for those "
"consuming the solutions on the cluster, and they may find it difficult to "
"filter an actionable event from the cluster. For more information, please "
"take a look at the [Kubernetes APIs convention](https://github.com/"
"kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-"
"conventions.md#events)."
msgstr "请注意，不建议为所有操作发出事件。如果作者发出过多事件，将对集群中使用解决方案的用户带来不好的用户体验，他们可能会发现很难从集群中过滤出可操作的事件。有关更多信息，请查阅 [Kubernetes API 约定](https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/devel/sig-architecture/api-conventions.md#events)。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:14
msgid "Writing Events"
msgstr "撰写事件"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:16
msgid "Anatomy of an Event:"
msgstr "事件的构成："

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:22
msgid "`object` is the object this event is about."
msgstr "`object` 是本事件所指的对象。"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:23
msgid ""
"`eventtype` is this event type, and is either _Normal_ or _Warning_. ([More "
"info](https://github.com/kubernetes/api/"
"blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/types.go#L6019-L6024))"
msgstr "`eventtype` 是事件类型，可以是 _Normal_ 或 _Warning_。 ([更多信息](https://github.com/kubernetes/api/blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/types.go#L6019-L6024))"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:24
msgid ""
"`reason` is the reason this event is generated. It should be short and "
"unique with `UpperCamelCase` format. The value could appear in _switch_ "
"statements by automation. ([More info](https://github.com/kubernetes/api/"
"blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/types.go#L6048))"
msgstr "`reason` 是生成此事件的原因。它应该简短且唯一，采用 `UpperCamelCase` 格式。该值可以在自动化的 _switch_ 语句中使用。 ([更多信息](https://github.com/kubernetes/api/blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/types.go#L6048))"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:25
msgid ""
"`message` is intended to be consumed by humans. ([More info](https://github."
"com/kubernetes/api/blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/"
"types.go#L6053))"
msgstr "`message` 是供人类使用的。 ([更多信息](https://github.com/kubernetes/api/blob/6c11c9e4685cc62e4ddc8d4aaa824c46150c9148/core/v1/types.go#L6053))"

#: src/reference/raising-events.md:32
msgid "Following is an example of a code implementation that raises an Event."
msgstr "以下是引发事件的代码实现示例。"

