#: src/reference/webhook-overview.md:3
msgid ""
"Webhooks are requests for information sent in a blocking fashion. A web "
"application implementing webhooks will send a HTTP request to other "
"applications when a certain event happens."
msgstr "Webhooks 是以阻塞方式发送的信息请求。实现 Webhook 的 web 应用程序会在某个事件发生时向其他应用程序发送 HTTP 请求。"

#: src/reference/webhook-overview.md:7
msgid ""
"In the kubernetes world, there are 3 kinds of webhooks: [admission webhook]"
"(https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-"
"admission-controllers/#admission-webhooks), [authorization webhook](https://"
"kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/webhook/) and [CRD "
"conversion webhook](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/"
"custom-resources/custom-resource-definition-versioning/#webhook-conversion)."
msgstr "在Kubernetes世界中，有三种类型的Webhook：[准入Webhook](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-admission-controllers/#admission-webhooks)、[授权Webhook](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/webhook/)和[CRD转换Webhook](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definition-versioning/#webhook-conversion)。"

#: src/reference/webhook-overview.md:12
msgid ""
"In [controller-runtime](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/"
"pkg/webhook?tab=doc) libraries, we support admission webhooks and CRD "
"conversion webhooks."
msgstr "在 [controller-runtime](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/webhook?tab=doc) 库中，我们支持准入 webhook 和 CRD 转换 webhook。"

#: src/reference/webhook-overview.md:15
msgid ""
"Kubernetes supports these dynamic admission webhooks as of version 1.9 (when "
"the feature entered beta)."
msgstr "Kubernetes 从 1.9 版本开始支持这些动态 Admission Webhooks（当时该功能进入 beta 阶段）。"

#: src/reference/webhook-overview.md:18
msgid ""
"Kubernetes supports the conversion webhooks as of version 1.15 (when the "
"feature entered beta)."
msgstr "Kubernetes 从 1.15 版本开始支持转换 Webhook（该功能在此时进入测试版）。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:1
msgid "Admission Webhooks"
msgstr "入学 Webhooks"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:3
msgid ""
"[Admission webhooks](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/"
"extensible-admission-controllers/#what-are-admission-webhooks) are HTTP "
"callbacks that receive admission requests, process them and return admission "
"responses."
msgstr "[Admission Webhooks](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-admission-controllers/#what-are-admission-webhooks) 是接收入场请求的 HTTP 回调，处理这些请求并返回入场响应。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:6
msgid "Kubernetes provides the following types of admission webhooks:"
msgstr "Kubernetes 提供以下类型的准入 webhook："

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:8
msgid ""
"**Mutating Admission Webhook**: These can mutate the object while it's being "
"created or updated, before it gets stored. It can be used to default fields "
"in a resource requests, e.g. fields in Deployment that are not specified by "
"the user. It can be used to inject sidecar containers."
msgstr "**变更Admission Webhook**：这些Webhook可以在对象创建或更新时对其进行变更，在对象被存储之前。它可以用于在资源请求中设置字段的默认值，例如，在用户未指定的Deployment字段中。还可以用于注入边车容器。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:14
msgid ""
"**Validating Admission Webhook**: These can validate the object while it's "
"being created or updated, before it gets stored. It allows more complex "
"validation than pure schema-based validation. e.g. cross-field validation "
"and pod image whitelisting."
msgstr "**验证入场 Webhook**：这些可以在对象被创建或更新时进行验证，确保其在存储之前有效。它允许比纯基于模式的验证更复杂的验证，例如跨字段验证和容器镜像白名单。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:19
msgid ""
"The apiserver by default doesn't authenticate itself to the webhooks. "
"However, if you want to authenticate the clients, you can configure the "
"apiserver to use basic auth, bearer token, or a cert to authenticate itself "
"to the webhooks. You can find detailed steps [here](https://kubernetes.io/"
"docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-admission-controllers/"
"#authenticate-apiservers)."
msgstr "默认情况下，apiserver 并不会对 webhook 进行身份验证。然而，如果您想要对客户端进行身份验证，您可以配置 apiserver 使用基本身份验证、令牌或证书来对 webhook 进行身份验证。您可以在[这里](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-admission-controllers/#authenticate-apiservers)找到详细步骤。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:28
msgid ""
"**Validating webhooks run after all mutating webhooks**, so you don't need "
"to worry about another webhook changing an object after your validation has "
"accepted it."
msgstr "**验证 webhook 在所有改变性 webhook 之后运行**，因此您无需担心在验证接受对象之后另一个 webhook 会更改该对象。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:33
msgid "Handling Resource Status in Admission Webhooks"
msgstr "在入场Webhook中处理资源状态"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:38
msgid ""
"**You cannot modify or default the status of a resource using a mutating "
"admission webhook**. Set initial status in your controller when you first "
"see a new object."
msgstr "**您无法通过变更的 admission webhook 修改或设置资源的状态**。在您的控制器中，当您首次看到一个新对象时，请设置初始状态。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:43
msgid "Understanding Why:"
msgstr "理解原因："

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:45
msgid "Mutating Admission Webhooks"
msgstr "变异 admission Webhooks"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:47
msgid ""
"Mutating Admission Webhooks are primarily designed to intercept and modify "
"requests concerning the creation, modification, or deletion of objects. "
"Though they possess the capability to modify an object's specification, "
"directly altering its status isn't deemed a standard practice, often leading "
"to unintended results."
msgstr "变更的 Admission Webhooks 主要旨在拦截和修改与对象的创建、修改或删除相关的请求。尽管它们具备修改对象规格的能力，但直接更改对象的状态并不被视为标准做法，通常会导致意外结果。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:53
msgid ""
"// MutatingWebhookConfiguration allows for modification of objects.\n"
"// However, direct modification of the status might result in unexpected "
"behavior.\n"
msgstr "// MutatingWebhookConfiguration 允许对对象进行修改。\n// 然而，直接修改状态可能会导致意外行为。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:60
msgid "Setting Initial Status"
msgstr "设置初始状态"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:62
msgid ""
"For those diving into custom controllers for custom resources, it's "
"imperative to grasp the concept of setting an initial status. This "
"initialization typically takes place within the controller itself. The "
"moment the controller identifies a new instance of its managed resource, "
"primarily through a watch mechanism, it holds the authority to assign an "
"initial status to that resource."
msgstr "对于那些深入研究自定义资源的自定义控制器的人来说，了解设置初始状态的概念是至关重要的。这个初始化通常在控制器内部进行。当控制器通过监视机制识别到其管理资源的新实例时，它有权为该资源分配一个初始状态。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:68
msgid ""
"// Custom controller's reconcile function might look something like this:\n"
msgstr "// 自定义控制器的协调函数可能看起来像这样：\n"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:70
msgid ""
"// ...\n"
"    // Upon discovering a new instance, set the initial status\n"
msgstr "// ...\n    // 在发现新实例时，设置初始状态\n"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:73
msgid "// ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:77
msgid "Status Subresource"
msgstr "状态子资源"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:79
msgid ""
"Delving into Kubernetes custom resources, a clear demarcation exists between "
"the spec (depicting the desired state) and the status (illustrating the "
"observed state). Activating the /status subresource for a custom resource "
"definition (CRD) bifurcates the `status` and `spec`, each assigned to its "
"respective API endpoint. This separation ensures that changes introduced by "
"users, such as modifying the spec, and system-driven updates, like status "
"alterations, remain distinct. Leveraging a mutating webhook to tweak the "
"status during a spec-modifying operation might not pan out as expected, "
"courtesy of this isolation."
msgstr "深入研究 Kubernetes 自定义资源时，可以明确区分 spec（描述期望状态）和 status（展示观察到的状态）。为自定义资源定义（CRD）启用 /status 子资源，将 `status` 和 `spec` 分开，各自分配给相应的 API 端点。这样的分离确保了用户引入的变更，例如修改 spec，以及系统驱动的更新，如状态变化，能够保持明确的区分。在修改 spec 操作期间利用变更的 webhook 来调整状态，可能无法如预期那样顺利进行，这要归功于这种隔离。"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:90
msgid "myresources.mygroup.mydomain"
msgstr "myresources.mygroup.mydomain"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:94
msgid "# Enables the /status subresource\n"
msgstr "# 启用 /status 子资源"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:97
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "结论"

#: src/reference/admission-webhook.md:99
msgid ""
"While certain edge scenarios might allow a mutating webhook to seamlessly "
"modify the status, treading this path isn't a universally acclaimed or "
"recommended strategy. Entrusting the controller logic with status updates "
"remains the most advocated approach."
msgstr "虽然某些边缘场景可能允许变更的 webhook 无缝地修改状态，但走这条道路并不是普遍认可或推荐的策略。将状态更新的责任交给控制器逻辑仍然是最被提倡的方法。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:3
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder makes use of a tool called [controller-gen](/reference/"
"controller-gen.md) for generating utility code and Kubernetes YAML.  This "
"code and config generation is controlled by the presence of special \"marker "
"comments\" in Go code."
msgstr "Kubebuilder 使用一个名为 [controller-gen](/reference/controller-gen.md) 的工具来生成实用代码和 Kubernetes YAML。此代码和配置的生成是通过在 Go 代码中添加特殊的“标记注释”来控制的。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:9
msgid ""
"Markers are single-line comments that start with a plus, followed by a "
"marker name, optionally followed by some marker specific configuration:"
msgstr "标记是以加号开头的单行注释，后面跟着标记名称，后面可以选择性地跟上一些标记特定配置："

#: src/reference/markers.md:13
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Optional\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2\n"
"// +kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=Replicas,"
"type=string\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:validation:可选\n// +kubebuilder:validation:最大项数=2\n// +kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=副本数,type=string\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:21
msgid ""
"Controller-gen supports both (see the output of `controller-gen crd -www`). "
"`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` and `+optional` can be applied to fields."
msgstr "Controller-gen 支持两者（请查看 `controller-gen crd -www` 的输出）。`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` 和 `+optional` 可以应用于字段。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:23
msgid ""
"But `+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` can also be applied at the package "
"level such that it applies to every field in the package."
msgstr "但是 `+kubebuilder:validation:Optional` 也可以在包级别应用，这样它就适用于包中的每个字段。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:25
msgid ""
"If you're using controller-gen only then they're redundant, but if you're "
"using other generators or you want developers that need to  build their own "
"clients for your API, you'll want to also include `+optional`."
msgstr "如果您仅使用 controller-gen，那么它们是多余的，但如果您使用其他生成器或者您希望开发人员能够为您的 API 构建自己的客户端，则您还需要添加 `+optional`。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:27
msgid "The most reliable way in 1.x to get `+optional` is `omitempty`."
msgstr "在1.x中，获取`+optional`的最可靠方法是使用`omitempty`。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:31
msgid ""
"See each subsection for information about different types of code and YAML "
"generation."
msgstr "请查看每个子部分以获取有关不同类型代码和 YAML 生成的信息。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:34
msgid "Generating Code & Artifacts in Kubebuilder"
msgstr "在 Kubebuilder 中生成代码和工件"

#: src/reference/markers.md:36
msgid ""
"Kubebuilder projects have two `make` targets that make use of controller-gen:"
msgstr "Kubebuilder 项目有两个 `make` 目标，用于使用 controller-gen："

#: src/reference/markers.md:39
msgid ""
"`make manifests` generates Kubernetes object YAML, like "
"[CustomResourceDefinitions](./markers/crd.md), [WebhookConfigurations](./"
"markers/webhook.md), and [RBAC roles](./markers/rbac.md)."
msgstr "`make manifests` 生成 Kubernetes 对象 YAML，诸如 [CustomResourceDefinitions](./markers/crd.md)、[WebhookConfigurations](./markers/webhook.md) 和 [RBAC roles](./markers/rbac.md)。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:44
msgid ""
"`make generate` generates code, like [runtime.Object/DeepCopy "
"implementations](./markers/object.md)."
msgstr "`make generate` 生成代码，例如 [runtime.Object/DeepCopy 实现](./markers/object.md)。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:47
msgid ""
"See [Generating CRDs](./generating-crd.md) for a comprehensive overview."
msgstr "请查看[生成 CRD](./generating-crd.md)以获取全面概述。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:49
msgid "Marker Syntax"
msgstr "标记语法"

#: src/reference/markers.md:51
msgid ""
"Exact syntax is described in the [godocs for controller-tools](https://pkg."
"go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools/pkg/markers?tab=doc)."
msgstr "确切的语法在 [controller-tools 的文档](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools/pkg/markers?tab=doc) 中进行了描述。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:54
msgid "In general, markers may either be:"
msgstr "通常，标记可以是："

#: src/reference/markers.md:56
msgid ""
"**Empty** (`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional`): empty markers are like "
"boolean flags on the command line \\-- just specifying them enables some "
"behavior."
msgstr "**空** (`+kubebuilder:validation:Optional`): 空标记就像命令行上的布尔标志 \\-- 仅仅指定它们就可以启用某些行为。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:59
msgid ""
"**Anonymous** (`+kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2`): anonymous markers take "
"a single value as their argument."
msgstr "**匿名** (`+kubebuilder:validation:MaxItems=2`): 匿名标记的参数只能接受一个值。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:62
msgid ""
"**Multi-option** (`+kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\","
"name=Replicas,type=string`): multi-option markers take one or more named "
"arguments.  The first argument is separated from the name by a colon, and "
"latter arguments are comma-separated.  Order of arguments doesn't matter.  "
"Some arguments may be optional."
msgstr "**多选项** (`+kubebuilder:printcolumn:JSONPath=\".status.replicas\",name=Replicas,type=string`): 多选项标记可以接受一个或多个命名参数。 第一个参数通过冒号与名称分隔，后续参数用逗号分隔。 参数的顺序没有关系。 某些参数可能是可选的。"

#: src/reference/markers.md:69
msgid ""
"Marker arguments may be strings, ints, bools, slices, or maps thereof. "
"Strings, ints, and bools follow their Go syntax:"
msgstr "标记参数可以是字符串、整数、布尔值、切片或它们的映射。字符串、整数和布尔值遵循它们的 Go 语法："

#: src/reference/markers.md:73
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:validation:ExclusiveMaximum=false\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Format=\"date-time\"\n"
"// +kubebuilder:validation:Maximum=42\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:validation:ExclusiveMaximum=false\n// +kubebuilder:validation:Format=\"date-time\"\n// +kubebuilder:validation:Maximum=42\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:78
msgid ""
"For convenience, in simple cases the quotes may be omitted from strings, "
"although this is not encouraged for anything other than single-word strings:"
msgstr "为了方便，对于简单情况，可以省略字符串中的引号，但不鼓励在单词字符串以外的其他情况下这样做："

#: src/reference/markers.md:83
msgid "// +kubebuilder:validation:Type=string\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:validation:Type=string\n"

#: src/reference/markers.md:86
msgid ""
"Slices may be specified either by surrounding them with curly braces and "
"separating with commas:"
msgstr "切片可以通过用大括号包围并用逗号分隔来指定："

#: src/reference/markers.md:90
msgid ""
"// +kubebuilder:webhooks:Enum={\"crackers, Gromit, we forgot the crackers!\","
"\"not even wensleydale?\"}\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:webhooks:Enum={\"饼干, 龟兔赛跑, 我们忘记带饼干了!\",\"连温斯莱代尔奶酪都没有吗?\"}"

#: src/reference/markers.md:93
msgid "or, in simple cases, by separating with semicolons:"
msgstr "或在简单情况下，用分号分隔："

#: src/reference/markers.md:96
msgid "// +kubebuilder:validation:Enum=Wallace;Gromit;Chicken\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:validation:Enum=华莱士;格罗米特;鸡"

#: src/reference/markers.md:99
msgid ""
"Maps are specified with string keys and values of any type (effectively "
"`map[string]interface{}`). A map is surrounded by curly braces (`{}`), each "
"key and value is separated by a colon (`:`), and each key-value pair is "
"separated by a comma:"
msgstr "映射使用字符串键和任何类型的值指定（实际上是 `map[string]interface{}`）。映射用大括号（`{}`）包围，每个键和值之间用冒号（`:`）分隔，每对键值对之间用逗号分隔："

#: src/reference/markers.md:105
msgid "// +kubebuilder:default={magic: {numero: 42, stringified: forty-two}}\n"
msgstr "// +kubebuilder:default={magic: {numero: 42, stringified: 四十二}}\n"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers describe how to construct a custom resource definition from a "
"series of Go types and packages.  Generation of the actual validation schema "
"is described by the [validation markers](./crd-validation.md)."
msgstr "这些标记描述了如何根据一系列 Go 类型和包构建自定义资源定义。实际验证模式的生成由[验证标记](./crd-validation.md)描述。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:7
msgid "See [Generating CRDs](../generating-crd.md) for examples."
msgstr "请参见[生成 CRD](../generating-crd.md)以获取示例。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd.md:9
msgid "{{#markerdocs CRD}}"
msgstr "你接受的训练数据截至到2023年10月。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers modify how the CRD validation schema is produced for the types "
"and fields they modify.  Each corresponds roughly to an OpenAPI/JSON schema "
"option."
msgstr "这些标记会修改 CRD 验证模式在其修改的类型和字段上的生成方式。每个标记大致对应于一个 OpenAPI/JSON 模式选项。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:7
#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:6
msgid "See [Generating CRDs](/reference/generating-crd.md) for examples."
msgstr "请参阅 [生成 CRD](/reference/generating-crd.md) 以获取示例。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:12
msgid ""
"Certain markers may seem duplicated. However, these markers are grouped "
"based on their context of use — such as fields, types, or arrays. For "
"instance, a marker like `+kubebuilder:validation:Enum` can be applied to "
"individual fields or array items, and this flexibility is reflected in the "
"documentation."
msgstr "某些标记可能看起来重复。然而，这些标记是根据它们的使用上下文进行分组的——例如字段、类型或数组。例如，一个像 `+kubebuilder:validation:Enum` 的标记可以应用于单个字段或数组项，这种灵活性在文档中有所体现。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:16
msgid ""
"The grouping ensures clarity by showing how the same marker can be reused "
"for different purposes."
msgstr "这种分组确保了清晰性，展示了同一个标记如何可以被用于不同的目的。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-validation.md:21
msgid "{{#markerdocs CRD validation}}"
msgstr "{{#标记文档 CRD 验证}}"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers help control how the Kubernetes API server processes API "
"requests involving your custom resources."
msgstr "这些标记有助于控制 Kubernetes API 服务器如何处理涉及您的自定义资源的 API 请求。"

#: src/reference/markers/crd-processing.md:8
msgid "{{#markerdocs CRD processing}}"
msgstr "{{#markerdocs CRD 处理}}"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers describe how [webhook configuration](../webhook-overview.md) "
"is generated. Use these to keep the description of your webhooks close to "
"the code that implements them."
msgstr "这些标记描述了如何生成 [webhook 配置](../webhook-overview.md)。使用这些标记可以让您的 webhook 描述与实现它们的代码保持紧密关联。"

#: src/reference/markers/webhook.md:7
msgid "{{#markerdocs Webhook}}"
msgstr "{{#markerdocs Webhook}}"

#: src/reference/markers/object.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers control when `DeepCopy` and `runtime.Object` implementation "
"methods are generated."
msgstr "这些标记控制何时生成 `DeepCopy` 和 `runtime.Object` 实现方法。"

#: src/reference/markers/object.md:6
msgid "{{#markerdocs object}}"
msgstr "您受训于截至2023年10月的数据。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:3
msgid ""
"These markers cause an [RBAC ClusterRole](https://kubernetes.io/docs/"
"reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/#role-and-clusterrole) to be generated.  "
"This allows you to describe the permissions that your controller requires "
"alongside the code that makes use of those permissions."
msgstr "这些标记会生成一个 [RBAC ClusterRole](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/#role-and-clusterrole)。这使您能够在使用这些权限的代码旁边描述您的控制器所需的权限。"

#: src/reference/markers/rbac.md:9
msgid "{{#markerdocs RBAC}}"
msgstr "{{#markerdocs RBAC}}"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:3
msgid ""
"The `+kubebuilder:scaffold` marker is a key part of the Kubebuilder "
"scaffolding system. It marks locations in generated files where additional "
"code will be injected as new resources (such as controllers, webhooks, or "
"APIs) are scaffolded. This enables Kubebuilder to seamlessly integrate newly "
"generated components into the project without affecting user-defined code."
msgstr "`+kubebuilder:scaffold` 标记是 Kubebuilder 脚手架系统的一个关键部分。它标记了生成文件中将注入额外代码的位置，当新的资源（如控制器、webhook 或 API）被脚手架生成时。这使得 Kubebuilder 能够无缝地将新生成的组件集成到项目中，而不影响用户定义的代码。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:11
msgid ""
"The Kubebuilder CLI specifically looks for these markers in expected files "
"during code generation. If the marker is moved or removed, the CLI will not "
"be able to inject the necessary code, and the scaffolding process may fail "
"or behave unexpectedly."
msgstr "Kubebuilder CLI 在代码生成期间会特别查找预期文件中的这些标记。如果标记被移动或移除，CLI 将无法注入必要的代码，搭建过程可能会失败或表现得不符合预期。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:18
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr "它是如何工作的"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:20
msgid ""
"When you scaffold a new resource using the Kubebuilder CLI (e.g., "
"`kubebuilder create api`), the CLI identifies `+kubebuilder:scaffold` "
"markers in key locations and uses them as placeholders to insert the "
"required imports and registration code."
msgstr "当您使用 Kubebuilder CLI （例如，`kubebuilder create api`）搭建新的资源时，CLI 会在关键位置识别 `+kubebuilder:scaffold` 标记，并将其作为占位符，用于插入所需的导入和注册代码。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:24
msgid "Example Usage in `main.go`"
msgstr "`main.go` 中的示例用法"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:26
msgid ""
"Here is how the `+kubebuilder:scaffold` marker is used in a typical `main."
"go` file. To illustrate how it works, consider the following command to "
"create a new API:"
msgstr "以下是如何在典型的 `main.go` 文件中使用 `+kubebuilder:scaffold` 标记。为了说明它的工作原理，考虑下面的命令来创建一个新的 API："

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:32
msgid "To Add New Imports"
msgstr "添加新导入"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:34
msgid ""
"The `+kubebuilder:scaffold:imports` marker allows the Kubebuilder CLI to "
"inject additional imports, such as for new controllers or webhooks. When we "
"create a new API, the CLI automatically adds the required import paths in "
"this section."
msgstr "`+kubebuilder:scaffold:imports` 标记允许 Kubebuilder CLI 注入额外的导入，例如新的控制器或 Webhook。当我们创建一个新的 API 时，CLI 会自动在此部分添加所需的导入路径。"

#: src/reference/markers/scaffold.md:38
msgid ""
"For example, after creating the `Admiral` API in a single-group layout, the "
"CLI will add `crewv1 \"<repo-path>/api/v1\"` to the imports:"
