#: src/reference/scopes.md:1
msgid "Understanding and Setting Scopes for Managers (Operators) and CRDs"
msgstr "理解和设定经理（操作员）及 CRD 的范围"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:3
msgid ""
"This section covers the configuration of the operational and resource scopes "
"within a Kubebuilder project. Managers(\"Operators\") in Kubernetes can be "
"scoped to either specific namespaces or the entire cluster, influencing how "
"resources are watched and managed."
msgstr "本节涵盖了在 Kubebuilder 项目中操作范围和资源范围的配置。Kubernetes 中的管理器（“操作员”）可以被限定在特定的名称空间或整个集群，从而影响资源的监视和管理方式。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:7
msgid ""
"Additionally, CustomResourceDefinitions (CRDs) can be defined to be either "
"namespace-scoped or cluster-scoped, affecting their availability across the "
"cluster."
msgstr "此外，自定义资源定义（CRDs）可以被定义为命名空间范围的或集群范围的，这会影响它们在集群中的可用性。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:11
msgid "Configuring Manager Scope"
msgstr "配置管理器范围"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:13
msgid ""
"Managers can operate under different scopes depending on the resources they "
"need to handle:"
msgstr "管理者可以根据他们需要处理的资源，在不同的范围内运作："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:16
msgid "(Default) Watching All Namespaces"
msgstr "（默认）监视所有命名空间"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:18
msgid ""
"By default, if no namespace is specified, the manager will observe all "
"namespaces. This is configured as follows:"
msgstr "默认情况下，如果未指定命名空间，管理器将观察所有命名空间。配置方式如下："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:27
msgid "Watching a Single Namespace"
msgstr "监视单一命名空间"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:29
msgid ""
"To constrain the manager to monitor resources within a specific namespace, "
"set the Namespace option:"
msgstr "要限制管理者在特定命名空间内监控资源，请设置命名空间选项："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:35
msgid "\"operator-namespace\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/scopes.md:40
msgid "Watching Multiple Namespaces"
msgstr "监视多个命名空间"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:42
msgid ""
"A manager can also be configured to watch a specified set of namespaces "
"using [Cache Config](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/"
"cache#Config):"
msgstr "管理员还可以通过[缓存配置](https://pkg.go.dev/sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/cache#Config)来配置以监视指定的命名空间集："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:49
msgid "\"operator-namespace1\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/scopes.md:50
msgid "\"operator-namespace2\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/scopes.md:56
msgid "Configuring CRD Scope"
msgstr "配置 CRD 范围"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:58
msgid ""
"The scope of CRDs determines their visibility either within specific "
"namespaces or across the entire cluster."
msgstr "CRD 的作用范围决定了它们是在特定命名空间内可见还是在整个集群中可见。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:60
msgid "Namespace-scoped CRDs"
msgstr "命名空间范围的自定义资源定义（CRD）"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:62
msgid ""
"Namespace-scoped CRDs are suitable when resources need to be isolated to "
"specific namespaces. This setting helps manage resources related to "
"particular teams or applications. However, it is important to note that due "
"to the unique definition of CRDs (Custom Resource Definitions) in "
"Kubernetes, testing a new version of a CRD is not straightforward. Proper "
"versioning and conversion strategies need to be implemented (example in our "
"[kubebuilder tutorial](https://book.kubebuilder.io/multiversion-tutorial/"
"tutorial)), and coordination is required to manage which manager instance "
"handles the conversion (see the official [kubernetes documentation](https://"
"kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-"
"definition-versioning/#webhook-conversion) about this). Additionally, the "
"namespace scope must be taken into account for mutating and validating "
"webhook configurations to ensure they are correctly applied within the "
"intended scope. This facilitates a more controlled and phased rollout "
"strategy."
msgstr "命名空间范围的 CRD（自定义资源定义）适用于当资源需要隔离到特定命名空间时。这种设置有助于管理与特定团队或应用程序相关的资源。然而，需要注意的是，由于 Kubernetes 中 CRD 的独特定义，测试 CRD 的新版本并非简单。需要实施适当的版本控制和转换策略（可参考我们的 [kubebuilder 教程](https://book.kubebuilder.io/multiversion-tutorial/tutorial)），并且需要协调管理哪个管理实例处理转换（有关此内容，请参阅官方 [kubernetes 文档](https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definition-versioning/#webhook-conversion)）。此外，必须考虑命名空间范围，以便在变更和验证 webhook 配置时确保它们在预期范围内正确应用。这将有助于实现更可控和分阶段的推出策略。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:67
msgid "Cluster-scoped CRDs"
msgstr "集群范围的 CRD（自定义资源定义）"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:69
msgid ""
"For resources that need to be accessible and manageable across the entire "
"cluster, such as shared configurations or global resources, cluster-scoped "
"CRDs are used."
msgstr "对于需要在整个集群中可访问和可管理的资源，例如共享配置或全局资源，使用集群范围的 CRD（自定义资源定义）。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:72
msgid "Configuring CRDs Scopes"
msgstr "配置 CRD 作用域"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:74
msgid "**When the API is created**"
msgstr "**当API被创建时**"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:76
msgid ""
"The scope of a CRD is defined when generating its manifest. Kubebuilder "
"facilitates this through its API creation command."
msgstr "在生成 CRD 的清单时定义其范围。Kubebuilder 通过其 API 创建命令来简化这一过程。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:79
msgid ""
"By default, APIs are created with CRD scope as namespaced. However, for "
"cluster-wide you use `--namespaced=false`, i.e.:"
msgstr "默认情况下，API 的 CRD 范围是命名空间级别的。然而，对于集群范围的 API，你可以使用 `--namespaced=false`，即："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:86
msgid ""
"This command generates the CRD with the Cluster scope, meaning it will be "
"accessible and manageable across all namespaces in the cluster."
msgstr "该命令生成具有集群范围的 CRD，这意味着它在集群中所有命名空间均可访问和管理。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:90
msgid "**By updating existing APIs**"
msgstr "通过更新现有的 API"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:92
msgid ""
"After you create an API you are still able to change the scope. For example, "
"to configure a CRD to be cluster-wide, add the `+kubebuilder:resource:"
"scope=Cluster` marker above the API type definition in your Go file. Here is "
"an example:"
msgstr "在您创建API之后，仍然可以更改其范围。例如，要将CRD配置为集群范围，请在您的Go文件中API类型定义上方添加`+kubebuilder:resource:scope=Cluster`标记。以下是一个示例："

#: src/reference/scopes.md:99
msgid ""
"//+kubebuilder:object:root=true\n"
"//+kubebuilder:subresource:status\n"
"//+kubebuilder:resource:scope=Cluster,shortName=mc\n"
msgstr "//+kubebuilder:object:root=true\n//+kubebuilder:subresource:status\n//+kubebuilder:resource:scope=Cluster,shortName=mc\n"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:106
msgid ""
"After setting the desired scope with markers, run `make manifests` to "
"generate the files. This command invokes [`controller-gen`](https://sigs.k8s."
"io/controller-tools) to generate the CRD manifests according to the markers "
"specified in your Go files."
msgstr "在设置好所需的范围和标记后，运行 `make manifests` 以生成文件。此命令会调用 [`controller-gen`](https://sigs.k8s.io/controller-tools) 根据您 Go 文件中指定的标记生成 CRD 清单。"

#: src/reference/scopes.md:111
msgid ""
"The generated manifests will then correctly reflect the scope as either "
"Cluster or Namespaced without needing manual adjustment in the YAML files."
msgstr "生成的清单将正确反映范围为集群或命名空间，而无需在 YAML 文件中手动调整。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:3
msgid ""
"This part describes how to modify a scaffolded project for use with multiple "
"`go.mod` files for APIs and Controllers."
msgstr "这部分描述了如何修改一个脚手架项目，以便与多个 `go.mod` 文件一起使用，用于 API 和控制器。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:5
msgid ""
"Sub-Module Layouts (in a way you could call them a special form of "
"[Monorepo's](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monorepo)) are a special use case "
"and can help in scenarios that involve reuse of APIs without introducing "
"indirect dependencies that should not be available in the project consuming "
"the API externally."
msgstr "子模块布局（可以称之为 [Monorepo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monorepo) 的一种特殊形式）是一个特殊的用例，可以在涉及重用 API 的场景中提供帮助，而不会引入不应在外部调用 API 的项目中出现的间接依赖。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:10
msgid ""
"If you are looking to do operations and reconcile via a controller a "
"Type(CRD) which are owned by another project or By Kubernetes API then, "
"please see [Using an external Resources/API](/reference/"
"using_an_external_type.md) for more info."
msgstr "如果您希望通过控制器对属于另一个项目或由 Kubernetes API 拥有的 Type（CRD）进行操作和对账，请参阅 [使用外部资源/API](/reference/using_an_external_type.md) 以获取更多信息。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:18
msgid ""
"Separate `go.mod` modules for APIs and Controllers can help for the "
"following cases:"
msgstr "为 APIs 和 Controllers 使用分开的 `go.mod` 模块可以帮助解决以下情况："

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:20
msgid ""
"There is an enterprise version of an operator available that wants to reuse "
"APIs from the Community Version"
msgstr "有一个企业版的 Operator 可用，它希望重用社区版的 API。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:21
msgid ""
"There are many (possibly external) modules depending on the API and you want "
"to have a more strict separation of transitive dependencies"
msgstr "有许多（可能是外部的）模块依赖于该 API，您希望对传递依赖关系进行更严格的分离。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:22
msgid ""
"If you want to reduce impact of transitive dependencies on your API being "
"included in other projects"
msgstr "如果您想减少传递依赖对您的 API 被其他项目包含的影响"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:23
msgid ""
"If you are looking to separately manage the lifecycle of your API release "
"process from your controller release process."
msgstr "如果您希望将 API 发布过程的生命周期与控制器发布过程分开管理。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:24
msgid ""
"If you are looking to modularize your codebase without splitting your code "
"between multiple repositories."
msgstr "如果您希望在不将代码分割到多个代码库的情况下对代码库进行模块化。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:26
msgid ""
"They introduce however multiple caveats into typical projects which is one "
"of the main factors that makes them hard to recommend in a generic use-case "
"or plugin:"
msgstr "然而，他们在典型项目中引入了多个警告，这是使它们在通用用例或插件中难以推荐的主要因素之一："

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:28
msgid ""
"Multiple `go.mod` modules are not recommended as a go best practice and "
"[multiple modules are mostly discouraged](https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/"
"Modules#faqs--multi-module-repositories)"
msgstr "多个 `go.mod` 模块并不被推荐作为 Go 的最佳实践，并且 [多个模块大多是不鼓励的](https://github.com/golang/go/wiki/Modules#faqs--multi-module-repositories)。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:29
msgid ""
"There is always the possibility to extract your APIs into a new repository "
"and arguably also have more control over the release process in a project "
"spanning multiple repos relying on the same API types."
msgstr "你总是可以将你的API提取到一个新的代码库中，并且在一个跨多个代码库、依赖于相同API类型的项目中，可能会对发布过程有更多的控制。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:30
msgid ""
"It requires at least one [replace directive](https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-mod-"
"file-replace) either through `go.work` which is at least 2 more files plus "
"an environment variable for build environments without GO_WORK or through "
"`go.mod` replace, which has to be manually dropped and added for every "
"release."
msgstr "它至少需要一个 [替换指令](https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-mod-file-replace)，要么通过 `go.work`（这至少需要两个以上的文件以及一个用于没有 GO_WORK 的构建环境的环境变量），要么通过 `go.mod` 替换，这需要在每次发布时手动添加和移除。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:35
msgid ""
"When deciding to deviate from the standard kubebuilder `PROJECT` setup or "
"the extended layouts offered by its plugins, it can result in increased "
"maintenance overhead as there can be breaking changes in upstream that could "
"break with the custom module structure described here."
msgstr "当决定偏离标准的 kubebuilder `PROJECT` 设置或其插件所提供的扩展布局时，可能会导致维护成本增加，因为上游可能会出现破坏性变化，这可能会与此处描述的自定义模块结构不兼容。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:37
msgid ""
"Splitting your codebase to multiple repos and/or multiple modules incurs "
"costs that will grow over time. You'll need to define clear version "
"dependencies between your own modules, do phased upgrades carefully, etc. "
"Especially for small-to-medium projects, one repo and one module is the best "
"way to go."
msgstr "将代码库拆分为多个仓库和/或多个模块会带来成本，并且这些成本会随着时间的推移而增加。你需要在自己的模块之间定义清晰的版本依赖关系，谨慎进行分阶段升级等。特别是对于小型到中型项目，一个仓库和一个模块是最佳选择。"

#: src/reference/submodule-layouts.md:39
msgid ""
"Bear in mind, that it is not recommended to deviate from the proposed layout "
"unless you know what you are doing. You may also lose the ability to use "
"some of the CLI features and helpers. For further information on the project "
"layout, see the doc [What's in a basic project?](./../cronjob-tutorial/basic-"
"project.md)"
msgstr "请记住，除非您知道自己在做什么，否则不建议偏离建议的布局。否则，您可能会失去使用某些 CLI 功能和助手的能力。有关项目布局的更多信息，请参阅文档 [基础项目包含哪些内容？](./../cronjob-tutorial/basic-project.md)"

